<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka two-year bonds issue oversubscribed.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka two-year bonds issue oversubscribed.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The auction for two-year Treasury Bonds worth 1.5 billion rupees with a coupon rate of 12.75 percent per annum held on Thursday was oversubscribed, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>Bids received totalled 1.88 billion rupees, of which bids at par amounted to 1.68 billion and bids at discount were 200 million.</p>
<p>	 Amount offered:	1,500 million rupees</p>
<p>	 Bids received:	 1,880 million rupees</p>
<p>	 Amount accepted:     1,500 million rupees</p>
<p>	 Weighted avg yield:  12.75 percent per year (current)</p>
<p>				    12.96 percent (previous)</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
